  "title": "# Tiny follow-up to PR #362 (md-chain-control) Brett: headless sessions should NOT start fresh per …",
  "asked": "# Tiny follow-up to PR #362 (md-chain-control) Brett: headless sessions should NOT start fresh per step. Change the shared registry default session mode from fresh-per-step to one session for the whole build (keep fresh-per-step as an option, not the default). Update the lean preset and any tests/docs that assume the old default. Push the commit onto branch claude/md-chain-control so PR #362 picks it up (git push origin HEAD:claude/md-chain-control, never force). Do not open a new PR, do not land. Read only the files you need; no full CLAUDE.md chain. ~10 minutes. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
